      "id": "factor-common-factorial",
      "title": "Factor out 7!",
      "explanation": "Both terms contain \\(7!\\), because \\(10!=7!\\cdot8\\cdot9\\cdot10\\). Also,\n\\[\n6!=1\\cdot2\\cdot3\\cdot4\\cdot5\\cdot6=720.\n\\]\nFactoring out \\(7!\\) gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n10!-7!\\cdot6!&=7!(8\\cdot9\\cdot10-6!)\\\\\n&=7!(720-720)=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{0}\\), choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
